{
	"title": "a process names no node by id: an id or a raw { path, part } given to a function is not-a-handle, and to land not a node handle [chee 10-25: \"i'm not sure the process api should be able to do anything by id\"]. land reaches the patch node by the handle it is sent (its maker's box: the handle carries it) or a path in the caller's box; protect is asked as the caller and as land, the target by its id, the patch node by the path it was made at, else its id. open (10-25): a policy by path on the target (deny edit secret from p) doesn't stop land, which asks the target by the id its patch names, though p's own edit(\"/secret\") is refused: land is looser than the caller's own functions there",
